<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Azov</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Azov is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rostov">Rostov</a> oblast, southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, on the Don near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-azov">Sea of Azov</a>. On the site of the medieval Italian trading post of Tana, it was an Ottoman fortress from 1475. Don <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossacks</a> seized it in 1637 and held it until 1642, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a> took it in 1696 but lost it in 1711, and it passed finally to Russia in the 18th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/azov.jpg" alt="Azov" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nadezhda1990 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%90%D0%B7%D0%BE%D0%B2_(%D0%A0%D0%BE%D1%81%D1%82%D0%BE%D0%B2%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B0%D1%8F_%D0%BE%D0%B1%D0%BB%D0%B0%D1%81%D1%82%D1%8C).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
